# Memory

Before starting any code task in rw-bess, before reading or editing source
files, read everything in:

```
~/.claude/memory/rw-bess
```

This path is the same for every rw-bess clone: `Documents/GitHub/rw-bess`,
`Projects/rw-bess`, and the per-ticket clones beside it.

Read every `.md` file directly in that folder. Do not sample or skim. Start
with `MEMORY.md`, the index. It holds durable context for this repo:
conventions, file locations, hardware and protocol details, and prior
decisions. Treat it as authoritative over assumptions inferred from the code.

Skip `archive/`. Those notes are superseded by these rule files or belong to
closed tickets. Read one only when the task names it.

If the folder is empty or missing, proceed normally.

Do not write to the memory folder unless explicitly asked.
